WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-IN

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.652
Hello Friends I am Mahesh from TrekBook India

00:00:09.652 --> 00:00:16.082
Todays topic is Top 5 Two-Wheeler insurance companies in India

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:19.503
so before we begin, let's see

00:00:19.503 --> 00:00:25.394
criteria's that I have considered to select best insurance

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:29.482
first &amp; foremost criteria is

00:00:29.482 --> 00:00:36.479
How strong is cashless garages network of insurance company

00:00:36.479 --> 00:00:40.896
this is very important since maximum 2-wheelers are there in India

00:00:40.896 --> 00:00:46.190
&amp; in case of accident, network garage is must for repairs

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:48.926
and to get cashless insurance without any hassle

00:00:48.926 --> 00:00:52.692
just submit the bike for repairs &amp; you get it back without paying any cash

00:00:52.692 --> 00:00:55.095
so this important point I have considered

00:00:55.738 --> 00:00:59.925
second is Which add-on rider options are given by company

00:00:59.925 --> 00:01:02.713
as an example - Zero Depreciation

00:01:02.713 --> 00:01:06.314
in case Plastic part brakes &amp; you don't have taken Zero Dep

00:01:06.314 --> 00:01:10.437
then you get only 50% cost of broken part

00:01:10.437 --> 00:01:14.036
so I will prefer to get Zero Dep cover by the company

00:01:14.036 --> 00:01:16.085
then accessories gets covered

00:01:16.085 --> 00:01:18.676
medical cover, passenger cover is there

00:01:18.676 --> 00:01:23.388
like in accident case driver &amp; passenger hospitalization expenses

00:01:23.388 --> 00:01:27.114
this can be also covered by insurance company as additional option

00:01:27.114 --> 00:01:28.611
so you should look at this option too

00:01:28.611 --> 00:01:31.724
Third point is How is the Customer Care Support?

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:37.515
you need to see if they have 24x7 attention line

00:01:37.515 --> 00:01:42.570
because anything can happen anytime &amp; getting timely help is important

00:01:42.570 --> 00:01:48.933
and main point again - coming to the Claim Settlement Ratio

00:01:48.933 --> 00:01:54.190
IRDA - Insurance Development Authority of India

00:01:54.190 --> 00:01:58.884
IRDA publishes data of claim settlement ratios by insurance companies

00:01:58.884 --> 00:02:01.660
so now I am moving on to the chart

00:02:01.660 --> 00:02:05.091
so I have taken an example at the top of chart

00:02:05.091 --> 00:02:11.119
my friends 2Wh Vespa VXL125 Std model, 125cc

00:02:11.119 --> 00:02:13.200
this is December 2016 model

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:15.615
for this I took out online quotations

00:02:15.615 --> 00:02:17.223
this is just a sample

00:02:17.223 --> 00:02:19.130
our main focus is not on example

00:02:19.130 --> 00:02:25.400
focus will be on which company is best based on criteria's which I told you

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:31.300
so first column is Insurance company name

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:37.409
second column belongs to claim settlement ratio in the year 2019-20

00:02:37.409 --> 00:02:38.578
this is IRDA data

00:02:38.578 --> 00:02:41.555
this I have taken from insurance dekho dot com website

00:02:41.555 --> 00:02:47.466
so indexing of table is done on that key

00:02:47.466 --> 00:02:50.444
means company having highest claim settlement ratio tops the list

00:02:50.444 --> 00:02:54.658
company  having lowest claim settlement ratio is at bottom of table

00:02:54.658 --> 00:02:59.173
chart have become slightly bigger, but t this time I have included each company

00:02:59.173 --> 00:03:04.739
during  my last car insurance video I skipped some companies &amp; people asked questions!

00:03:04.739 --> 00:03:10.467
now see that third party cover highlighted in blue colour 

00:03:10.467 --> 00:03:12.861
so that is common across all

00:03:12.861 --> 00:03:16.377
because the third party insurance price is fixed price

00:03:16.377 --> 00:03:21.787
so 752 Rs in this case is constant for all companies

00:03:21.787 --> 00:03:26.277
previous column is IDV Insured Declared Value

00:03:26.277 --> 00:03:29.936
means How much amount you will get if your bike gets 100% damage

00:03:29.936 --> 00:03:34.513
this is flexible &amp; you can increase it, but then premium will go up accordingly

00:03:34.513 --> 00:03:36.739
third column is Zero Depreciation cover

00:03:36.739 --> 00:03:38.403
if you wish, you can take that

00:03:38.403 --> 00:03:40.352
it will add to some charges

00:03:40.352 --> 00:03:42.715
&amp; then road toe assistance

00:03:42.715 --> 00:03:47.632
so personally as per me Zero Dep &amp; Road toe assistance is better to take

00:03:47.632 --> 00:03:50.518
so if you take both these riders

00:03:50.518 --> 00:03:54.037
so rider will have added cost depending on company to company

00:03:54.037 --> 00:03:57.866
&amp; finally it comes out to Total Package Premium

00:03:57.866 --> 00:03:59.955
over &amp; above you have 18% GST

00:03:59.955 --> 00:04:04.945
so second last column will have amount to be paid

00:04:04.945 --> 00:04:08.551
last column shows the network garages

00:04:08.551 --> 00:04:11.219
so how many network garages a company have?

00:04:11.219 --> 00:04:17.818
so considering all these I have numbered top companies

00:04:17.818 --> 00:04:20.036
&amp; why that I want to tell you

00:04:20.036 --> 00:04:25.378
so I have given number 1 for SBI General insurance

00:04:25.378 --> 00:04:26.522
there are 2 reasons for that

00:04:26.522 --> 00:04:31.075
one is their Claim settlement ration is 90%

00:04:31.075 --> 00:04:35.953
second they have highest 16K+ network garages

00:04:35.953 --> 00:04:43.707
so compared to other companies SBI Gen have both claim settlement ratio &amp; network garages good

00:04:43.707 --> 00:04:46.987
that is the reason I have sleeted them at Number 1

00:04:46.987 --> 00:04:51.283
Number 2 is HDFC General Ergo Insurance

00:04:51.283 --> 00:04:54.595
their Claim settlement ratio is 91.23%

00:04:54.595 --> 00:04:56.066
and

00:04:56.066 --> 00:04:59.265
